  let right = arr.length - 1;

  while (left <= right) {
    const mid = Math.floor((left + right) / 2);

    if (arr[mid] === target) {
      return mid;
    } else if (arr[mid] < target) {
      left = mid + 1;
    } else {
      right = mid - 1;
    }
  }

  return -1; // Element not found
}
```

This function takes two parameters: `arr`, which is the sorted array to be searched, and `target`, which is the element we want to find. It initializes `left` as the first index of the array and `right` as the last index of the array.

